#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:42
msgid "When you suggest a feature while you are logged in, we store that the request came from your account. When you suggest a feature without an account, you can give your name and email address. We store them with your request. Only our team can see them, and we use them only to contact you about your request. A request is public once we approve it, without your name."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: name of a cookie.
#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:45
#, php-format
msgid "When you vote while you are logged in, we store your vote with your account. When you vote without an account, we store a cookie named %s in your browser for one year, so that the site remembers your votes. The cookie holds a random number and nothing else about you."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:48
msgid "When you are logged in and you vote for a request, suggest one or press its Follow button, we store that you follow that request, and we email you when its status changes. Every email has a link that stops these emails, and you can also stop them in your profile."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy/PolicyText.php:49
msgid "To limit how often one visitor can vote or send requests, we count attempts per IP address for up to one hour. The count is stored under a scrambled form of the address that cannot be turned back into it. We do not store your IP address."
msgstr ""

